== ESTIMATED removable turn-cell squared error in the 210 under each consistent definition (HYPOTHESIS where marked)
  M2b_s0: turn-cell SSE in the 210 = 1733.5 (phi 0.189); route-speaks RMSE = 0.410
    (L) LABEL-side: null the turn cells of non-announced events (CURVE + SUPPRESSED = 177 windows): metric loses 1410.1 = 81.3% of the 210's turn-cell SSE = phi 0.154. This moves the METRIC, not the driving; it also removes the (possibly useful) curve-geometry supervision.
    (N1) NAV-side, like-for-like: let the nav speak for the 37 silent is_turn windows (longer lookahead / no suppression): error to the route-speaks level frees 85.2 = 4.9% of the 210's SSE = phi 0.009  [ESTIMATED; needs the nav to supply the ego's own future path = optimistic]
    (N2) NAV-side, announce CURVES too: if T reached the junction-turn error on curves, frees 1078.5 = 62.2% of the 210's SSE = phi 0.117  [HYPOTHESIS: the 0.40 level was measured on slow tight junction turns only; and it hands T the future path of the ego]
  M2b_s1: turn-cell SSE in the 210 = 1683.6 (phi 0.181); route-speaks RMSE = 0.396
